---
import Section from './Section.astro';
import { site } from '../config';

const roles = [
  {
    when: 'Kakao',
    title: 'Android, web, desktop, and cloud',
    body: 'Led development in a team of more than twenty supporting 45M+ monthly users, and built Korea’s largest map service with street-view VR.',
  },
  {
    when: 'StellarStep',
    title: 'Founder, 2014 to 2018',
    body: 'Founded and bootstrapped a mobile computer vision venture.',
  },
  {
    when: 'Commerzbank',
    title: 'Lead software engineer, 2019 to 2025',
    body: 'Rebuilt the payment core of a mobile banking app with 19.8M active installs, part of a roughly €700M digital transformation, under BaFin, GDPR, and PSD2.',
  },
];
---

<Section
  id="founder"
  label="Founder"
  title="Taeho Lee, founder of the SSCCS initiative"
  lede="He is the architect of the addressing primitive that Ktema commercializes, and the author of three preprints published between February and August 2026."
>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      His engineering stack covers C and C++, Rust, chip design and verification (RTL),
      compilers, and distributed systems. He has worked in software since 2008.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="cards cards--3">
    {
      roles.map((role) => (
        <div class="card">
          <span class="card__value">{role.when}</span>
          <h3>{role.title}</h3>
          <p>{role.body}</p>
        </div>
      ))
    }
  </div>

  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      Ktema is the product he sells. It stands on the SSCCS stack, the result of nine months of
      self-funded work that produced the engine, the proofs, and the hardware decoder. He runs
      the agent runtime that operates the engineering work, and he is the first engineer of the
      system.
    </p>
    <p>
      The first hire follows the first design partner, and it is field-facing: someone who sits
      in front of firmware teams and handles integration. The embedded buyer is also buying an
      answer to a ten-year question, which is who fixes this bug in 2036.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p class="links"><a href={site.linkedin}>LinkedIn</a> · <a href={site.github}>GitHub</a></p>
</Section>

<style>
  .links {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--ink-3);
  }
</style>
